{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "What is Object Oriented Programming?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about Object Oriented Programming"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Build the macro system conceptual model following the customer requirements, through the use and interpretation of collected information, represented in class diagrams, interaction diagrams, and operation contracts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple present tense in affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">Simple present tense in affirmative</span>  to talk about a topic, regular action or fact."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Follow this structure when you use the <span class= \"strong\">simple present</span>,  tense in affirmative: <br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + verb + complement</div><br><br>  When you use the pronouns <span class= \"strong\">I, you, we</span>, and <span class= \"strong\">they</span>, you simply use the infinite form of the main verb without the preposition to. <br><br> Example: <br> We <span class= \"strong\">implement </span>  software technology that permits us to handle data more easily. <br><br>  When you use the pronouns <span class= \"strong\">she, he</span>, and <span class= \"strong\">it</span>, you need to add <span class= \"strong\">\u2013s, -es</span>, or <span class= \"strong\">\u2013ies</span>, depending on the case, at the end of the main verb. Take a look at the explanation below. <br><br> <ul> <li> You add <span class= \"strong\">\u2013s</span>  to verbs finishing in a consonant, verbs ending in a vowel + <span class= \"strong\"> y</span>, and verbs finishing in vowel e. For example: permit<span class= \" strong \"> s, say<span class= \" strong \"> s, and realize<span class= \"strong\"> s</span>. </li>  <li>You add <span class= \"strong\">\u2013es</span>  to verbs ending in o, s, ss, sh, zz, ch, and x. For example: <span class= \"italic\"> go <span class= \"strong\">es</span>, pass <span class= \"strong\">es</span>, wash <span class= \"strong\">es</span>, buzz<span class= \" strong \"> es</span>, catch<span class= \" strong \"> es</span>, and fax<span class= \" strong\"> es</span></span>. </li>  <li>You add <span class= \"strong\">\u2013ies</span>  to verbs ending in consonant y. <span class= \"italic\"> For example: stud <span class= \"strong\">ies</span></span> </li> </ul> <br> <br> Examples:<br> <span class= \"italic\"> Software technology <span class= \"strong\">permits</span> us to handle technology more easily.<br> Our manager <span class= \"strong\">does</span> an appropriate analysis before making a decision. <br> Our company <span class= \"strong\">classifies</span> information with the help of a software</span>. <br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Remember that the effectiveness of our system depends on how efficient is our software model."}, {"type": "example", "content": "OOP describes the manipulation of data."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Can in Affirmative Statements"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">can in affirmative statements</span>  to talk about possibilities"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class= \"strong\"> can </span> to talk about permission, possibility, or ability.<br><br>  You use the <span class= \"strong\"> modal can </span> following this structure: <br><br>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + can + verb + complement</div> <br><br> When you use the modal verb <span class= \"strong\"> can </span>, remember two things: <br>1. the main verb doesn't change its spelling; it maintains its infinitive form. <br>2. You can use any subject with it. <br><br>  Example: <br> <span class= \"italic\"> You can create a simple software to store data related to your customers' information using OOP. <br> Our company can organize the input and output information. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't really know how I can implement that system in my company."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You can come up with a simplified abstract model that facilitates techniques to get useful output data."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "software"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a series of useful instructions to perform specific functions"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In this case, you can create a simple software to store data related to your customers' information using OOP."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "OOP"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "object oriented programming"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(acronym)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: OOP has data associated, classes and objects; and it has also the behavior associated that is the computer program that helps us to codify data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "codify"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to organize and present information and instructions in a simplified way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In that way I can organize the input and output information. And it saves us time. But, OOP needs to codify all the data, right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "input data"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information received"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can come up with a simplified abstract model that facilitates techniques to get useful output data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "output data"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information produced "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can come up with a simplified abstract model that facilitates techniques to get useful output data."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "paradigm"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "structure and style of programming that represents a sample model"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: OOP is a method or programming paradigm which create objects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look up about Class and Object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a definition for Class and Object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a chart to explain the difference between them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with your teacher and partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I understand what Class and Object is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write definitions of Class and Object."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I recognize the difference between them. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my chart with the rest of the class."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Classes and Objects"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">classes</span>  and <span class=\"strong\">objects</span> to differentiate properties from general to specific when creating an object oriented program."}, {"type": "text", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">class</span>  is a software that presents all the general properties of data that the software is manipulating. </br></br> Individual <span class= \"strong\"> objects</span>  are those specific properties that a class created as particular parts within class software."}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob01img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"id": 0, "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>CEO</strong>: As you can see, I created a model to manipulate the input of data in my company, but now I hear everybody talks about OOP and I don't really know how I can implement that system in my company. <br/>\n<strong>Consultant</strong>: Well, you just need to transform that model into a computer system. In this case, you can create a simple software to store data related to your customers' information using OOP. <br/>\n<strong>CEO</strong>: I don't even know what OOP is."}, {"time": "29000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Consultant</strong>: OOP is a method or programming paradigm which creates objects that model the business issue we want to solve. OOP identifies and describes data to be used.<br/>\n<strong>CEO</strong>: But, what do I need OOP for?<br/>\n<strong>Consultant</strong>: You can come up with a simplified abstract model that facilitates techniques to get useful output data. <br/>\n<strong>CEO</strong>: Oh! That is what we call abstraction. I can look at the real world and simplify that into a codified software. That way, I can organize the input and output information; that saves us time. But, OOP needs to codify all the data, right?<br/>"}, {"time": "71000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Consultant</strong>: Well, OOP uses classes and objects. For example, let's pretend I have a bank account that is individual and specific; you can say that it is an object. Then, every single person has his own bank account; it means there are many objects in just one class or issue. So, in general terms, the class in this specific example is the group of those bank accounts.<br/>\n<strong>CEO</strong>: So, OOP has data associated, classes and objects, and it also has a behavior associated that is the computer program that helps us codify data. Now, I have individual and general data from customers, and I need to know the program that develops the OOP for my company.<br/>\n<strong>Consultant</strong>: Remember that the effectiveness of the software depends on how the input and output data is handled."}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what Object Oriented Programming is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss simple real world examples to understand OOP."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about abstraction to create a computer system in OOP."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think computer systems are able to codify huge amounts of information? How?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you think you can manage and store data in an effective way?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "How can computer programming make your life easier?"}], "questions": [], "img_path": ""}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "A business consultant advices a <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">CEO </span>to organize the information of his company"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "You're done!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"tip_id": 0, "type": "text", "content": "\u201c<span class=\"italic\">CEO</span>\u201d refers to the Chief Executive Officer or the Boss of a company"}]}], "questions": [{"_